#: cards:1
msgid "Name of Document"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Naming the document"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"<p>The <strong>Label</strong> (required) is the name shown in search results"
" and on the public site. For a manuscript, use <code>City. Library, Ms. "
"N</code>, e.g. <code>Avranches. Bibliothèque municipale Edouard Le Héricher,"
" Ms. 59</code>. The label can hold an English and a French text; give both "
"when they differ.</p><p>Set <strong>Type</strong> to « preferred terms » for"
" the main name and to « alternate titles » for other forms of it (e.g. "
"<code>Avranches. BM, Ms. 59</code>); « translated titles » is for a "
"translation. Fill <strong>Language</strong> when the name belongs to one "
"language (the main name of MS 59 is French); it is not needed otherwise.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Name of Person"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Naming the person"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"<p>Enter one name per entry in <strong>Label</strong>, spelled as in your "
"source and in one form for every record (<em>Forename Surname</em>, ordinary"
" capitals), e.g. <em>Hildegard of Bingen</em>, then the other forms of the "
"same person (<em>Hildegard von Bingen</em>) as further entries.</p><p>Set "
"<strong>Type</strong> to « preferred terms » for the main name, « alternate "
"titles » for variants and « translated titles » for translations. Give the "
"<strong>Language</strong> when you record several forms of the name, so they"
" can be told apart; a single name does not need it.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Imaging layers"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "What each canvas of the imaging manifest shows"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Describing the imaging layers"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"<p>One entry per canvas (image) of this manifest, to say what the image shows. The <strong>Canvas id</strong> is the <code>@id</code> of the canvas in the manifest (open <code>/manifest/&lt;id&gt;</code> and copy it); the <strong>Canvas label</strong> is the label stored in the manifest, a reading aid only.</p>\n"
"<p><strong>Content</strong> says what the layer represents. An element map: the <strong>Element(s)</strong> (several for a composite) and, for X-ray maps, the <strong>Emission line</strong>. A spectral band: the <strong>Band</strong> value and unit, the bounds only for a range. A statistical component: the <strong>Processing</strong> method and the <strong>Component index</strong>.</p>\n"
"<p>The acquisition technique is the one of the analysis (card « Technique used »). <strong>Processing</strong> is needed only when the layer is not as acquired: deconvolved, normalised, a ratio, a false-colour composite (give the channels in <strong>Inputs</strong>), a PCA/MNF/ICA component, a classification.</p>\n"
"<p>The Analysis Explorer reads only these entries, never the canvas labels.</p>\n"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Naming the group"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"<p>Enter one name per entry in <strong>Label</strong>. Give the official "
"name in its own language as « preferred terms », e.g. <em>Abbaye du Mont-"
"Saint-Michel (ordre monastique)</em>; a parenthesis only tells homonyms "
"apart or names the body's kind or parents, as in <em>Centre de la Recherche "
"sur la Conservation (CNRS / MNHN / Ministère de la Culture)</em>.</p><p>Add "
"the other forms as further entries: « translated titles » for a translation,"
" e.g. <em>Abbey of Mont-Saint-Michel (monastic order)</em> with "
"<strong>Language</strong> « English (language) », « alternate titles » for "
"variants. Give the <strong>Language</strong> when you record several forms; "
"a single name does not need it.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Name of Place"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Naming the place"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"<p>Enter one name per entry in <strong>Label</strong> (required), in the "
"form your source gives. For the main name, add a qualifier in brackets when "
"it removes doubt: <em>Avranches (Normandie)</em>, <em>France (nord)</em>. "
"Other names of the same place (<em>Paris (France)</em>) go in further "
"entries.</p><p>Set <strong>Type</strong> to « preferred terms » for the main"
" name, « alternate titles » for variants and « translated titles » for "
"translations. Fill <strong>Language</strong> when a form belongs to one "
"language (e.g. « French (language) »); it is not needed otherwise. Use "
"<strong>Source</strong> for the record that attests the name, when one "
"exists.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Mapbox API"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Represents a single node in a graph"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"Arches uses the Mapbox mapping library for map display and data creation.  "
"Arches also supports Mapbox basemaps and other services"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Joining Group event"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Date of joining"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"<p>A joining is usually dated approximately, so give a range: « between 1130"
" and 1140 » is the earliest possible date in the required "
"<strong>Date</strong> (the begin) and the latest possible date in "
"<strong>Date (end of the end)</strong>, as <code>YYYY-MM</code> or a year "
"alone. With the choice above them, mark the dates « Approximative » when "
"they are not certain, « Confirmed » when they are.</p><p>For a finer "
"reading, the four fields are: begin (<strong>Date</strong>), latest begin "
"(<strong>Date (end of the begin)</strong>), earliest end (<strong>Date (end "
"approximative)</strong>) and latest end (<strong>Date (end of the "
"end)</strong>). When only the period is known, use the sub-card below.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Naming the alteration"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"<p>The <strong>Label</strong> is the name shown in search results; build it "
"so it can be read alone: <code>&lt;phenomenon&gt; - &lt;zone&gt; "
"&lt;folio&gt; - &lt;shelfmark&gt;</code>, with a plain hyphen between the "
"three parts, the zone and the folio joined by a space, and the shelfmark "
"written <code>BM Avranches MS 59</code> for this manuscript. The label can "
"be entered in English and in French.</p><p>Set <strong>Type</strong> to « "
"preferred terms » for the main name, and to « alternate titles » or « "
"translated titles » for the others, one entry each. "
"<strong>Language</strong> is rarely needed: fill it only for a name written "
"in a language other than English or French.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Name of Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Naming the analysis"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"<p>The <strong>Label</strong> is the name shown in search results and on the"
" public site, so it must read alone. Recommended form: <code>&lt;analysis "
"code&gt; - &lt;zone&gt; &lt;folio&gt; - &lt;shelfmark&gt;</code>, with a "
"plain hyphen between the three parts, the zone and the folio joined by a "
"space, and the shelfmark written <code>BM Avranches MS 59</code> for this "
"manuscript. The technique is not part of the name; it has its own "
"card.</p><p>Set <strong>Type</strong> to « preferred terms » for the main "
"name. Add a translated or alternate name as a further entry; give its "
"<strong>Language</strong> when the name exists in several languages.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Name of Component"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid "Naming the component"
msgstr ""

#: cards:1
msgid ""
"<p>The <strong>Label</strong> (required) is the name shown in search results"
" and on the public site. Build it so it can be read alone: "
"<code>&lt;zone&gt; &lt;folio&gt; - &lt;shelfmark&gt;</code>, the zone and "
"the folio joined by a space (no hyphen between them), the folio as "
"<code>f31v</code>, and a plain hyphen before the shelfmark, written <code>BM"
" Avranches MS 59</code> for this manuscript. E.g. <code>Parchment f31v - BM "
"Avranches MS 59</code>.</p><p>Set <strong>Type</strong> to « preferred terms"
" » for the main name; add other names as further entries. "
"<strong>Language</strong> is rarely needed: fill it only for a name written "
"in one language.</p>"
msgstr ""

